 "notes": "Boundary of the WD initial-final mass relation (IFMR) exclusion region on g_agamma vs ALP mass. Curve extracted from the vector paths of Figure 17 (Section4/Figures/WDIFMR_rotn.pdf in the e-print), taking the light-blue curve that includes the paper's conservative 0.08 Msun upward IFMR shift for rotational mixing/core overshoot, which the paper adopts as its final result (Section 4.6) and which matches the WD-IFMR region shown in the concluding Figure 18 (Param_concl.pdf). The excluded region lies to the left of/inside this boundary: the points run along the lower edge from 1 keV (g~1.6e-10 GeV^-1) up to the maximum-mass tip at ~575 keV (g~3e-6), then back along the upper (ALP-decay-relaxed) edge to ~81 keV where the curve exits the plotted range at g=1e-3 GeV^-1; the list is therefore ordered along the boundary path, not monotonically in mass. Axes calibrated from tick positions of the vector PDF. Stellar (AGB energy-loss) bound: no dark-matter density assumed. The paper does not quote a formal confidence level for its bound (it excludes couplings for which the theoretical IFMR falls outside the full range of the Andrews et al. double-white-dwarf posterior IFMRs); 0.95 entered as the closest schema value.",
